[thinking] The anatomy shows LC4 feeding strongly into DNp01, DNp02, DNp04, and DNp11, with DNp04 receiving over 
half of GF input, while LPLC2 also connects to DNp01 and DNp04. I want to check DNa02's steering role for turning 
away, plus DNp04, DNp11, and the backward-signaling MDN, and trace how LC4 connects to DNa02.

Now I'm setting up a physiology simulation: stimulating LC4 and LPLC2 on the left side only, then watching how 
DNp01, DNp02, DNp04, DNp11, DNa02, MDN, and DNg40 respond. I'll run the descriptions of DNp04, DNp11, DNa02 
alongside the LC4→DNa02 path trace in parallel.



